# Committed readings for realloc-wait-late.wasm and its control realloc-wait-late-ctl.wasm (#994; the chair's
# ruling of 2026-10-18, item 4). Default path: gate:async on, no host, no Threads.
# Built:       wasm-tools parse <name>.wat -o <name>.wasm   (wasm-tools 1.258.0; both validate with --features all)
# Invocation:  wasmtime run -W component-model-threading=y -W component-model-async=y --invoke 'res()' <name>.wasm
# Engine:      wasmtime 49.0.3 (f96eabaa1 2026-10-14), darwin/arm64.
#
# reader                                      realloc-wait-late                        realloc-wait-late-ctl
# wasmtime 49.0.3, 10 of 10 each              trap: cannot leave component instance    3
# Burroughs at fc0bd9b, 3 of 3                waits out the park's 30s bound           3
# Burroughs with #994's fix, 3 of 3           trap: wswait … may not leave (immediate)  3
#
# Meaning:     the child YIELDs before task.return, so the parent's async lower returns STARTED and the result
#              store runs later, when the child resolves. The store lowers a string through the parent's
#              realloc, which calls waitable-set.wait. A realloc runs with may_leave = False
#              (LiftLowerContext.reallocate), so the reference traps inside the store. The control's realloc
#              does not wait, so its late store succeeds and res() returns the string's length.
#
#              Before the fix the store's failure set a variable nothing read once the lower had returned, so
#              the subtask never resolved and the parent's WAIT expired with "waitable set 2 produced nothing
#              in 30s". The fix routes it as a trap to the caller's task, which owns the subtask (ADR 0101's
#              Option A, point 7). The reference ends the whole store; ending the caller's task is the subset
#              owner routing gives, and #1040 records the remaining difference.
#
#              realloc-wait.wasm's res() is the same shape with a child that resolves in its first segment.
#              Since #1034's F0 that store runs inside the lower, so its failure was already the lower's trap,
#              and it no longer reached #994.
